[NOTE] The "ETA" on the lines above is an ARTIFACT, ignore it. It computes
       elapsed / rows_reported, but a row only counts when its whole SHARD
       finishes, and all 8 workers began on their largest shard (the driver
       sorts descending for LPT bin packing). So for the first ~15 min the
       numerator holds 8 workers' wall time while the denominator holds 1
       worker's output, inflating the ETA by roughly 8x.
       Scaling from the first real datapoint (hp7-k33: 403 rows at k=33 in
       13.7 min of one worker = 3.91% of the corpus cost-weight) the true
       figure is 0.7-1.2 h wall, depending on whether per-row cost grows
       like k^2 or k^1.1. Expect the reported ETA to fall steeply as the
       big first shards land together.
